//! The `block_drops` hooks and helpers: declarations the mod API generator reads (see `hooks/mod.rs`).

pub trait Hooks {
    /// NeoForge's `BlockDropsEvent`: a block `state` broke at `pos` and `Block.dropResources` has built the item entities `drops` it will spawn, but nothing is in the world yet. `breaker` is the breaking player's UUID (none for a break the level makes: a piston, water, a neighbour update, `/setblock destroy`) and `tool` the stack they used (none when no tool). `breaker_entity` is the entity that broke the block (NeoForge's `getBreaker()`): the player, or the mob whose own break of this block is running (a ravager's, a wither's). It is none when no entity broke it: a piston, water, a neighbour update, `/setblock destroy` and explosions. `block_entity` is the block's block entity (NeoForge's `getBlockEntity()`), none for a block without one and for explosions (their blocks are already gone). For a player's break the removal has already taken the block entity out of the world, so its saved data, read before the removal (its `CustomName` too), is held through the event: `level.block_entity_data(entity)` reads it, and the handle is stale (reads refuse) once the event ends, also if a listener panics. `drops` is the list `Block.popResource` built: each stack with the position, motion and pickup delay its item entity will have, drawn before the event as vanilla draws them, so the level random's order does not depend on whether a mod listens. Edit the list (take out, change or add drops; empty stacks don't spawn) or `experience`, the points `spawnAfterBreak` would award at the block's centre (ores, sculk, spawners; silk touch has already zeroed it, as NeoForge's description says, "the true value, after enchantments"). Set `cancel` and nothing spawns: no drops, no experience, and none of `spawnAfterBreak`'s other effects (an infested block's silverfish); a bee nest's bees are `playerDestroy`'s, not `spawnAfterBreak`'s, and still come out. With the `block_drops` rule off the list and the experience are emptied after the event. It fires on the player's break, a mob's block break that drops loot, explosions and every level-side `Block.dropResources` (a piston breaking a block, water washing one away, a removed support). Player, explosion and mob block loot passes through `loot_drops` first; level-side breaks are not asked `loot_drops`. Explosion events run after the blast has removed its blocks and merged their loot, before any items spawn, with no breaker or tool and zero initial experience. Each block's event owns only its share of a merged stack, at that entity's prepared position and velocity; cancellation cannot remove another block's share. Unchanged shares rejoin the original merged entity, while edited or added entities spawn exactly as returned. Even a block with no loot gets an event (TNT that primes instead does not). Neither registration nor a no-op listener changes the merge or the level random's draws. It does not fire for dispensers or a block's own loot-table drop through another path. It runs inside the level's write, so the level host reads blocks and draws the level's random in vanilla's order and writes nothing. Authoritative servers only. Replaces `block_exp`, whose catalog row named no NeoForge event (`none`) and fired only on the level-side path: the amount is `experience` here. Diverges from upstream: `block_exp` is removed into this hook.
    #[notes = r#"## Block drops

- **`block_drops(level, dimension, pos, state, breaker, breaker_entity, block_entity, tool, drops, experience, cancel)`** (NeoForge's `BlockDropsEvent`): `Block.dropResources` built the item entities for a broken block and nothing has spawned yet. Edit `drops` (`ItemDrop`: stack, position, velocity, pickup delay, and the item entity's thrower, target, no-gravity and starting age) or `experience`, or set `cancel` for no drops, no experience and no `spawnAfterBreak` effects (an infested block's silverfish; a bee nest's bees are `playerDestroy`'s and still come out). `breaker` is the player's UUID, none for a level-side break; `breaker_entity` is the entity that broke it (the player, or the mob whose own break runs; none for a piston, water, a neighbour update, `/setblock destroy` and explosions) and `block_entity` the block's block entity (none for a block without one and for explosions). After a player's break removed it, its saved data (with `CustomName`) is held through the event: `level.block_entity_data(entity)` reads it, and the handle is stale once the event ends, also after a listener panic; `tool` is their stack. It fires on the player's break, mob block breaks that drop loot, explosions and every level-side `Block.dropResources`. Positions and motions are drawn before the event, in vanilla's order, listener or not, and the list is the one that spawns, so a mod that leaves it alone changes nothing. It runs inside a level write, so it gets the level host: reads and the level's random, no writes. Player, mob and explosion block loot still runs `loot_drops` first; a level-side break is not asked `loot_drops`. Not fired for dispensers or other loot-table drops. Explosions start with zero experience, but a listener may award it. Their events run after the blast removes the blocks and merges loot, before items spawn. Each block owns only its contribution to a merged entity, with that entity's prepared position and velocity: cancel removes only that share. Unchanged shares rejoin the original merged entity; edited or added drops spawn exactly as returned. Empty-loot blocks still fire; TNT that primes instead does not. A no-op listener preserves both merging and level-random draws. Tick-time effect: explosions add a `listened` branch per block; contribution tracking allocates only with listeners. Mob breaks use the same item construction and XP sampling as other block breaks. Level-side breaks and explosion loot fire it too. Diverges from upstream: `block_exp` is removed into `experience` (its catalog row named no NeoForge event)."#]
    #[hook(
        side = "server",
        contract = "cancel",
        out = "cancel",
        neoforge = "BlockDropsEvent",
        cancellable = true,
        version = 2,
        target = "horizon_client::game::native_hooks::block_drops::GameLevel<'_>::native_block_drops"
    )]
    fn block_drops(
        dimension: LevelDimension,
        pos: BlockPos,
        state: BlockState,
        breaker: Option<u128>,
        breaker_entity: Option<EntityRef>,
        block_entity: Option<BlockEntityRef>,
        tool: Option<&ItemStack>,
        drops: &mut Vec<ItemDrop>,
        experience: &mut u32,
        cancel: &mut bool,
    );
}
